  "worked_solution": "Starting at the origin, we move along the $x$ and $y$ axes to get to the point $A.$\n\nFirst, we move along the $x$-axis. The point $A$ has an $x$-coordinate of $-3,$ so we move $3$ units to the *left*, in the *negative* direction of the $x$-axis.\n\nThen, we move along the $y$-axis. The point $A$ has a $y$-coordinate of $4,$ so we move $4$ units *up*, in the *positive* direction of the $y$-axis.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14129504/assets/d5143459ae5b0e9704d8faa67dd3acf429832b668eae21ef9ca9e031e551432f.png)",
